cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or reference its experimental simulation results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Blockchain-Assisted Privacy-Preserving Federated Learning for Network Intrusion Detection with Trust-Based Security and Cryptographic Auditing"
abstract: >-
  A Python-based research simulation platform for network intrusion detection on
  NSL-KDD, integrating single-process federated learning (five simulated clients
  with Non-IID Dirichlet partitioning), client-level differential privacy
  (OS-CSPRNG Gaussian perturbation and Renyi Differential Privacy accounting),
  privacy-aware multi-criteria trust calibration against Byzantine poisoning, a
  locally simulated tamper-evident SHA-256 and ECDSA audit ledger, and an
  interactive Streamlit dashboard.
repository-code: "https://github.com/RanvyGHBs/blockchain-fl-ids"
url: "https://github.com/RanvyGHBs/blockchain-fl-ids"
authors:
  - family-names: "Thakur"
    given-names: "Ranveer Singh"
keywords:
  - federated-learning
  - differential-privacy
  - intrusion-detection
  - pytorch
  - blockchain
  - cybersecurity
  - streamlit
  - machine-learning
